From fd3a82b163e5d881dd3848759963d399f20de4e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:02:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remote room members across machines: a target-issued,
 revocable, policy-bound capability (H658 partial)

A member of a room can live on another Nerva hub and act on this one under a grant this
hub issued and can revoke. Off unless JARVIS_ROOM_PEERS.

- Transport: the member hub POSTs to /api/room-peers/peer/{accept,call,renew} through
  the governed egress client (room-peers manifest). Ed25519 identity keys pinned both
  ways; every request signed (method/path/ts/nonce/body/grant, 60 s window, replay
  cache) and every response signed back and verified. No hub token opens a peer route.
- Membership: invitation is a roompeer.invite ask card; the one-time bundle exists only
  after approval; accept needs the code proof and the member key's signature, is single
  use and bumps the room's authority epoch.
- Grant: Authorization: NervaRoom <grant>, HMAC by this hub, scoped to room, epoch,
  member and target, bound to an execution-policy digest (tool allowlist with live
  gating, permissions, call budget). Revocation, epoch and digest checked on every call;
  renewal refused on digest mismatch.
- Execution: each dispatch crosses this hub's Action Kernel as
  roommember:<room>:<member>@<hub> (room.remote_call, kill-switch scope room:<id>,
  broker token); read-only runs inline via ToolRPC, gated becomes a roompeer.call card
  re-checked at execution. Audit on both sides.
- Owner UX: admin /api/room-peers routes, `nerva rooms`, Console Remote Members panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
